Cell[TextData[{
 "An object with edges is drawn as a line, the stroke along each edge growing \
with its count; any other object as dots on its vertices, sized by mass. A \
mass of 1 draws at the substrate's own vertex size and edge thickness, in the \
object's colour; the heaviest mass of an object draws at the top of the \
range, by default 3 times the base size for a dot and 4 times for a stroke. \
The opacity follows mass over the heaviest mass, along ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<OpacityRange\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b9a1dc6-71b7-4b33-b3d3-161a185bd6b1"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7e1fa267-634f-41cf-afee-b3fa1ebbed9f"],

Cell["\<\
A negative mass is drawn as an empty ring, a positive one as a filled dot; a \
zero mass is not drawn.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"19fe5801-af84-48f7-9d4d-5397f9d3f317"],

Cell["\<\
Where objects overlap, their strengths add and their colours blend.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"db8febc3-184d-41aa-8255-a09d38e88d3a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the list, a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Directive"]], "paclet:ref/Directive"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6030d4cd-108e-4346-a667-2e9c0af3a99a"],
 " styles every object after it, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"obj", " ", "->", " ", "style"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "87474bb9-1b1c-4faf-94b0-d887e3660d50"],
 " one object. A colour there replaces the palette colour."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b7d9c147-8b2c-4b9b-9344-0058654b70f6"],

